From f31b4d485bbd4191ea76862e3d8945c3798af2f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Regner <nathanregner@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 2 May 2026 11:00:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Add proxy-based authentication for trusted reverse proxy
 deployments

When running Hydra behind a trusted reverse proxy (e.g., nginx with
Tailscale), this allows automatic authentication based on HTTP headers
set by the proxy, eliminating the need for password login.

Configuration via <proxy_auth> block in hydra.conf:
- user_header: HTTP header containing username (default: X-Remote-User)
- roles: static roles to assign (no default - must be explicit)
- roles_header: HTTP header for dynamic role assignment
- auto_create_user: create users on first access (default: 1)
- disable_password_login: block /login endpoint (default: 0)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
